# Relaxations of the range checks, planted one at a time by scripts/relaxation-check.
# Each line: name | file | function | text replaced | replacement | times replaced
# The text is matched inside the named function only. An empty replacement removes it.
# A line "not planted: name | reason" is printed by the check and not run.
# A relaxation that does not apply, or that no property test fails on, fails the check.

# The root jump is hashed as given, so it must be the leading bits of the key.
root jump not compared with the key | lib/aiken/csmt.ak | after_root_jump | expect slice_bytearray(0, rj_len, key_bits) == root_jump | | 1
root jump compared with the key by length only | lib/aiken/csmt.ak | after_root_jump | expect slice_bytearray(0, rj_len, key_bits) == root_jump | expect rj_len <= bytearray.length(key_bits) | 1

# The steps must end at the start of the key: key bits left over would be unhashed.
inclusion walk may leave key bits unconsumed | lib/aiken/csmt.ak | fold_including | expect cursor == 0 | | 1
inclusion walk may leave one key bit unconsumed | lib/aiken/csmt.ak | fold_including | expect cursor == 0 | expect cursor <= 1 | 1
extremum inclusion walk may leave key bits unconsumed | lib/aiken/csmt.ak | fold_including_extremum | expect cursor == 0 | | 1
extremum inclusion walk may leave one key bit unconsumed | lib/aiken/csmt.ak | fold_including_extremum | expect cursor == 0 | expect cursor <= 1 | 1

# Every step consumes at least one key bit.
inclusion step may consume any number of key bits | lib/aiken/csmt.ak | fold_including | expect consumed >= 1 | | 1
inclusion step may consume no key bits | lib/aiken/csmt.ak | fold_including | expect consumed >= 1 | expect consumed >= 0 | 1
# The extremum walk repeats this check on its own steps; it is listed, not planted.
not planted: extremum inclusion step may consume any number of key bits | redundant through the public API: every caller also runs the same steps through fold_including, which refuses them
not planted: extremum inclusion step may consume no key bits | redundant through the public API: every caller also runs the same steps through fold_including, which refuses them
exclusion step above the lowest may consume any number of key bits | lib/aiken/csmt.ak | do_excluding | expect next_step.consumed >= 1 | | 1
exclusion step above the lowest may consume no key bits | lib/aiken/csmt.ak | do_excluding | expect next_step.consumed >= 1 | expect next_step.consumed >= 0 | 1

# The sibling that takes the removed branch's place keeps the key bits above the branch.
exclusion sibling drops the key bits between the branches | lib/aiken/csmt.ak | collapse | slice_bytearray(above, bottom_cursor - above, key_after_root) | #"" | 1

# Every byte of a jump is a bit; a larger byte would carry into the bits before it.
jump byte not checked to be 0 or 1 | lib/aiken/csmt/bits.ak | pack_one_byte | expect bit <= 1 | | 1
jump byte allowed up to 2 | lib/aiken/csmt/bits.ak | pack_one_byte | expect bit <= 1 | expect bit <= 2 | 1
